INTRODUCTION:

Sterling Service Bulletin Board System
for the Amiga.
The following features should be noted:

        >  Allows text files to be written as "descriptions" of uploaded
           files, similar to some of the national computer services.
        >  Zmodem file transfer protocol (including batch download)
        >  Doors (90% compatible with Paragon* doors)
        >  24 Flags for User and Sysop security access
        >  6 "clubs", each independent of the others, with 8 sections
           in each to aid file & message organization
        >  Two levels of Sysop for added security & convenience
        >  Four separate menu sets, allowing the use of different
           text and color graphic interfaces for the user.
        >  Locked Baud rates
        >  User choice of Line or VT100 Screen Editor for messages.

Features new to version 1.2 include a point-and-click graphic interface for
the local Sysop, and support for high-speed (eg. MNP) modems.

The BBS, of which this is a Demo, is easy to set-up and operate. There is
no compiling of menus, or other complicated set-ups. Customization is done
via an Intuitionized, point-and-click control-panel! This file now
includes a demo of this program, "Demo.Create". Note that both Load and
Save functions are disabled in the Create demo!  Simply double-click the
icon to view the program.

In addition, for those converting from BBS-PC**, utilities are supplied
to convert your users and download list to Sterling Service format.

This Demo isn't intended to be a full Bulletin Board, and should NOT be run
unattended (not all files/functions are supported)!  It's sole purpose is
to give you an idea what the BBS looks like before deciding whether or
not to purchase it.

